sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant W as WebhookController
    participant K as Kafka (meeting.events)
    participant MC as MeetingEventConsumer
    participant MS as MeetingService
    participant TS as TranscriptService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over C,DB: Edge case — two concurrent sessions of the SAME meeting, tracked independently

    C->>W: POST meeting.started (meeting=M, session=A)
    W->>K: publish (key = A)
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>MS: handleMeetingStarted
    MS->>DB: upsert Meeting M, create Session A (LIVE)

    C->>W: POST meeting.started (meeting=M, session=B)
    W->>K: publish (key = B)
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>MS: handleMeetingStarted
    MS->>DB: Meeting M exists, create Session B (LIVE)

    C->>W: POST transcript (session=A)
    W->>K: publish (key = A)
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>TS: handleTranscript
    TS->>DB: insert segment under Session A

    C->>W: POST transcript (session=B)
    W->>K: publish (key = B)
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>TS: handleTranscript
    TS->>DB: insert segment under Session B

    C->>W: POST meeting.ended (session=A)
    W->>K: publish (key = A)
    K->>MC: deliver
    MC->>MS: handleMeetingEnded
    MS->>DB: Session A → ENDED (Session B stays LIVE)
    Note right of MS: sessionId is the unit of isolation.<br>Segments and lifecycle are per-session under one Meeting.
